# fuzz/.gitignore — emitted by scripts/campaign-init.sh on fresh scaffold.
#
# Intent (PLUGIN_ISSUES.md friction item 4 — "do not delete the only backup of
# untracked work"):
#
#   The Mosquitto campaign had fuzz/findings/ untracked. A "productionization
#   cleanup" deleted the sole .bak of a working PoC variant, forcing
#   reconstruction from memory. Keeping findings/ TRACKED by default makes the
#   git history the backup — a clobber requires `git reflog` to recover, not
#   recovery-from-nothing.
#
#   The broad fuzz/* ignore here intentionally excludes large ephemeral state
#   (corpus, harness binaries, coverage tracefiles, fuzzer logs) from the
#   repo — but findings/ and findings.jsonl carry the disclosure work and MUST
#   stay tracked. Negate them with !findings/ and the matching tree.
#
# DO NOT add `findings/` (or any negated path here) to a top-level .gitignore
# without ALSO updating this file. The negation has to live in the deepest
# .gitignore for git to honor it.

# Default: ignore everything under fuzz/ (large, regeneratable, churn-y).
*

# But keep .gitignore itself tracked so the rules survive a re-init.
!.gitignore

# Keep the high-value disclosure work tracked — this is the load-bearing line.
!findings/
!findings/**

# Keep the campaign's structured state tracked. These files are small and
# carry the audit trail (findings.jsonl, plan.md, events.jsonl, the schema'd
# JSONs the agents read between ticks). The .trash/ subtree (backup-safe
# staging from findings.sh and cleanup scripts) is intentionally NOT
# negated — it's local salvage, not history.
!state/
!state/findings.jsonl
!state/plan.md
!state/harnesses.json
!state/harness-built.json
!state/current.json
!state/fuzz-config.json
!state/dropped_crashes.jsonl
!state/harness-corrections.jsonl

# Keep the nix campaign-flake deps file tracked (campaign-init writes it).
!nix-deps.nix

# Keep the gitignore template's own footprint visible.
!.trash/.gitkeep
